From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:14:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: Ocarina of Time past its
 2010-0212 stop, stub replies zeroed (upstream Lichii)

With its mesh draws skipped, Ocarina of Time reached gameplay on PS5-680 twice and stopped both
times within seconds (67 s and 59 s): it calls prepo:u 10500, which no core implements, and the
auto stub replied with the result only. The game read its reply words anyway, took its own
request's leftover "SFCI" for an object id (HasSessionRequestHandler: object_id 1229145683 is too
big), and panicked with 2010-0212. The owner's desktop Lichii (nx2-build-130) logs the same call
and plays on: upstream's c26cfaeac4 (Takoroka, 1 November) replies with 32 zeroed words after the
result, after the core this port pins. Core patch 0077 does the same for both of the auto stub's
replies.
---
 .../0077-stub-replies-zeroed.patch            | 49 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tools/eglantine-patches/0077-stub-replies-zeroed.patch

diff --git a/tools/eglantine-patches/0077-stub-replies-zeroed.patch b/tools/eglantine-patches/0077-stub-replies-zeroed.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a79cb03
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/eglantine-patches/0077-stub-replies-zeroed.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp b/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp
+index cdc5d35..50ad26d 100644
+--- a/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp
++++ b/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp
+@@ -67,6 +67,22 @@ void ServiceFrameworkBase::RegisterHandlersBaseTipc(const FunctionInfoBase* func
+         handlers_tipc.emplace_hint(handlers_tipc.cend(), functions[i].expected_header, functions[i]);
+ }
+ 
++namespace {
++
++// Callers read the reply words they expect without checking how many were written, so an empty
++// reply hands them the request's leftover words as data (an HDR output format, a refresh rate, a
++// device id; Ocarina of Time's prepo:u 10500 took its own request's "SFCI" for an object id and
++// stopped with 2010-0212). Stub replies carry this many zeroed words (upstream c26cfaeac4).
++constexpr u32 StubZeroedWords = 32;
++
++void PushStubZeroes(IPC::ResponseBuilder& rb) {
++    for (u32 i = 0; i < StubZeroedWords; ++i) {
++        rb.Push<u32>(0);
++    }
++}
++
++} // namespace
++
+ void ServiceFrameworkBase::ReportUnimplementedFunction(HLERequestContext& ctx,
+                                                        const FunctionInfoBase* info) {
+     // EDEN_NX2_AUTO_STUB=1 auto-stubs every unknown command without touching the config. Switch 2
+@@ -83,8 +99,9 @@ void ServiceFrameworkBase::ReportUnimplementedFunction(HLERequestContext& ctx,
+         static std::set<std::pair<std::string, u32>> reported;
+         std::scoped_lock lk{reported_mutex};
+         if (!reported.emplace(service_name, ctx.GetCommand()).second) {
+-            IPC::ResponseBuilder rb{ctx, 2};
++            IPC::ResponseBuilder rb{ctx, 2 + StubZeroedWords};
+             rb.Push(ResultSuccess);
++            PushStubZeroes(rb);
+             return;
+         }
+     }
+@@ -104,8 +121,9 @@ void ServiceFrameworkBase::ReportUnimplementedFunction(HLERequestContext& ctx,
+     UNIMPLEMENTED_MSG("Unknown / unimplemented {}", fmt::to_string(buf));
+     if (auto_stub) {
+         LOG_WARNING(Service, "Using auto stub fallback (repeats of this command are not logged)");
+-        IPC::ResponseBuilder rb{ctx, 2};
++        IPC::ResponseBuilder rb{ctx, 2 + StubZeroedWords};
+         rb.Push(ResultSuccess);
++        PushStubZeroes(rb);
+     }
+ }
+ 
